1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,313
One month into your new budget, and it didn't go to plan?

2
00:00:03,733 --> 00:00:09,295
Good. That's normal. Month one is for finding out what's true. Here's how to fix it, with real numbers.

3
00:00:10,065 --> 00:00:12,382
Let's review our example from episode one.

4
00:00:13,152 --> 00:00:15,297
Step one. Put planned next to actual.

5
00:00:15,717 --> 00:00:16,591
Here's the month.

6
00:00:17,011 --> 00:00:19,335
Groceries and gas ran $120 over.

7
00:00:19,755 --> 00:00:21,279
Fun money, $60 over.

8
00:00:21,699 --> 00:00:23,400
Utilities came in $30 under.

9
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:26,721
And an oil change nobody planned for, $75.

10
00:00:27,141 --> 00:00:28,975
Net: $225 over plan.

11
00:00:29,395 --> 00:00:34,044
That came out of the goal money, so only $132 reached the credit card this month.

12
00:00:34,814 --> 00:00:37,111
Step two. Fix the numbers, not yourself.

13
00:00:37,531 --> 00:00:38,398
Four fixes.

14
00:00:38,818 --> 00:00:43,429
Groceries were planned too low. Make it $700, a number you can actually hit.

15
00:00:43,849 --> 00:00:49,531
Fun money stays at $200, but it moves to its own card or cash, so you can see it running out.

16
00:00:49,951 --> 00:00:56,052
The oil change wasn't a surprise. Add $10 a paycheck to your surprise funds for car upkeep.

17
00:00:56,472 --> 00:00:59,869
And leave utilities alone. One cheap month isn't a trend.

18
00:01:00,289 --> 00:01:04,665
New goal money: $277 a month. Lower than before. But it's real.

19
00:01:05,085 --> 00:01:07,467
The perfect plan cleared the card in eight months.

20
00:01:07,887 --> 00:01:11,486
The real plan takes ten, and about sixty dollars more in interest.

21
00:01:11,906 --> 00:01:17,235
Two extra months beats quitting in February. A budget you keep beats a perfect one you abandon.

22
00:01:18,005 --> 00:01:24,318
The Paycheck Planner in the description makes these changes in seconds. Change one number, and everything updates.

23
00:01:24,738 --> 00:01:27,364
Subscribe, and keep going. Month two is easier.
